=== morning ===
# speaker:mbah_hita
# script:morning
The ground wakes before you do, Nak. I checked.
* [Ask what needs doing.]
    Water what you planted. Leave a little room for shade later. A place can feed you and still feel asri.
    -> END
* [Say you were already awake.]
    Of course. Your eyes were simply resting while the hoe waited.
    -> END

=== day ===
# speaker:mbah_hita
# script:day
Do not rush to fill every empty corner. A good yard needs somewhere for the wind to pass.
* [Ask about his plan.]
    Trees, water, useful ground, and a seat where nobody is hurried away. That is enough to begin.
    -> END
* [Promise to remember.]
    Remember with your hands, not only your head. The soil can tell the difference.
    -> END

=== evening ===
# speaker:mbah_hita
# script:evening
Listen. When the road quiets, you can hear how much this place still needs.
* [Ask what he hears.]
    Dry leaves, an empty channel, and one impatient grandchild. The last one is improving.
    -> END
* [Sit with him for a moment.]
    Good. Work that never stops is only another kind of noise.
    -> END
